solution:
**Given: **

81x⁻³ ÷ 81⁴ = sqrt[6]{9²⁴}

**Formula used:**

am ÷ aⁿ = am⁻ⁿ

(am)ⁿ = amⁿ

sqrt[n]{x} = x⁽¹⁾/⁽ⁿ⁾

If ax = ay, then x = y

**Calculation:**

81x⁻³ ÷ 81⁴ = sqrt[6]{9²⁴}

⇒ 81x⁻³⁻⁴ = sqrt[6]{9²⁴}

⇒ 81x⁻³⁻⁴ = sqrt[6]{9²⁽¹²⁾}

⇒ 81x⁻³⁻⁴ = sqrt[6]{81¹²}

⇒ 81x⁻³⁻⁴ = {81⁽¹²⁾/⁽⁶⁾}

⇒ 81x⁻³⁻⁴ = 81²

Now, on comparing the power with same base, we get,

⇒ x - 3 - 4 = 2

⇒ x - 7 = 2

⇒ x = 9

**∴ The required value of 'x' is 9.**
